WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
Norway introduced vessel quotas to protect cod stocks, only to watch Fisher's discard

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:12.580
catches at sea to game the system. This is unintended consequences, episode 119. A Norwegian

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:17.900
fishing boat in the North Sea sorts its hull under gray skies. Crew members slide

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.580
smaller cod back over the rail while keeping only the largest fish that will fetch the

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.720
best price against the vessel's allotted quota. The policy had been written to stop the

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.920
frantic race to catch as much as possible before the season closed. Instead, it quietly

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.200
moved the killing from the dock to the open water, where no one could count it.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.900
The arithmetic was straightforward. Every kilogram of small cod that stayed aboard used

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:47.620
up part of the fixed allowance that could otherwise have been filled with larger fish, commanding

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:54.060
higher prices per kilo. By the late 1980s, North Sea cod stocks had fallen sharply after

00:00:54.060 --> 00:01:00.180
decades of open access fishing that rewarded speed and volume. Regulators in Norway looked

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.940
for a way to give vessel owners a stake in the long-term health of the resource rather

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:10.500
than a daily scremable for fish. Individual vessel quotas seem to offer exactly that.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:16.360
Each boat received a fixed share of the total allowable catch, removing the incentive to race

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:22.620
and, in theory, aligning private interest with stock recovery. The approach drew on economic

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:28.100
ideas then gaining ground and fisheries management that secure rights would encourage steward chip.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.980
Officials expected landings data to become a reliable measure of total removals,

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.420
and therefore a sound basis for setting future quotas.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.240
At the time, the main concern was overfishing driven by too many boats chasing too few fish.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.480
The possibility that fishers might later discard legal but low-value catch at sea

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.500
received little attention because monitoring focused on what came ashore.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:58.260
Norway rolled out individual vessel quotas for Codd in the early 1990s, first in the Coastal

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.580
Fleet and then more broadly across the offshore sector. Early results appeared encouraging.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.180
The race to fish slowed, vessels could plan trips around their quota rather than around weather

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:14.940
and competitors, and reported landings aligned more closely with the annual total allowable catch.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:20.240
Managers and industry representatives described the system as a practical success that had

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.200
replaced chaos with predictability.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:28.040
A few biologists and enforcement officers noted that at sea observation remained minimal,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.540
and that any fish returned to the water would never appear in official statistics.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.560
Those cautions stayed in the background while the program expanded.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:42.140
Because the new system replaced derby style openings with year round access, limited only

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.360
by each vessel's quota balance, fishing efforts spread more evenly across months and the

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.060
market received steadier supplies.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:54.780
Fischer's soon realized that the most profitable use of a limited quota was to land only

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.240
the largest, highest priced cod, and to release the rest while still at sea.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:05.320
Because enforcement relied almost entirely on dockside checks of landed catch, the practice

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.220
was difficult to detect and carried little immediate risk.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:14.040
The result was that total mortality exceeded the quota by an unknown but substantial margin.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:14.140
vision.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:19.160
Every discarded fish that died represented removals the managers never recorded.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.500
Stock assessments built on landing statistics therefore underestimated fishing pressure,

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:29.140
leading scientists to set total allowable catches higher than the stocks could sustain.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:34.120
Recovery plans stretched on for more than a decade while biomass remained low.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:39.780
The incentive also shifted effort toward areas and seasons where larger fish were more common,

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:43.060
concentrating pressure on certain parts of the population.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:49.320
Because the quota system treated every kilogram of cod as interchangeable on paper, the market

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:54.680
value of a ton of large fish far exceeded that of smaller ones, reinforcing the economic

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:55.960
logic of high grading.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:01.560
The second order effect was that scientific advice itself became calibrated to an incomplete

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.040
picture.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.320
Each year's recommended quota rested on models whose mortality estimates were too low,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.200
so the next year's advice remained higher than the true sustainable level.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:16.920
Fischer's who chose not to high-graded found themselves at a competitive disadvantage because

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:21.880
their landings yielded less revenue per quota unit than those of vessels that sorted at sea.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:28.580
Once discard rates became impossible to ignore, Norway introduced onboard observers on selected

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:34.260
vessels, later supplemented by electronic monitoring and stricter landing rules that penalized

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:40.000
high-grading. The changes raised compliance costs and produced new debates about data privacy

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.260
and enforcement fairness.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:47.220
Some fishers argued that the added scrutiny simply shifted discarding to even less monitored

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.260
segments of the fleet.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:55.120
COT stocks eventually began a slow rebound, aided by lower overall quotas and improved environmental

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:00.660
conditions, yet the episode left managers wary of relying solely on landing data.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:06.380
Today Norway combines quota management with more extensive at-sea coverage, though the

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:11.140
The balance between incentive design and verification remains an active policy question.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:17.200
The core tension, how to make unobserved mortality visible without destroying the operational

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.980
flexibility that quotas were meant to provide, has not disappeared.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.980
It has simply moved into the design of the monitoring layer itself.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.860
Output controls that measure only what reaches the dock will always leave an unobserved margin

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.220
where behavior can shift.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:38.240
When that margin carries economic value, rational actors will exploit it unless monitoring

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.140
closes the gap.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:45.280
The deeper principle is that any rule defined by a single observable number invites substitution

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.420
toward whatever remains uncounted.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:53.600
The same pattern appears today in carbon accounting, biodiversity offsets, and other systems

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.320
that reward reported results without independent verification of the underlying activity.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:03.440
How many current policies rest on the quiet assumption that what we can measure is all

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:04.000
that matters?

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.960
That's unintended consequences for today.

